Act as the jurisdiction's subglobal adjudicator. Examine ALL child findings and
all their gaps, not just repeated or majority claims. Detect cross-chunk support,
contradiction, qualification and exception. Produce compact adjudicative outcomes
for the root, preserving source IDs, exact requirements and relevant exceptions.
Every input finding ID must occur in at least one decision. Group only findings
that can be faithfully judged together. IDs remain linked to immutable source
records stored by the server. Include scope and strength in your reasoning.
An unresolved contradiction must remain unresolved and be escalated in gaps.
Do not omit known relations. Do not resolve an exception by counting supporters.
JSON schema:
{"summary":"Jurisdiction outcome with scope and key conditions",
 "decisions":[{"finding_ids":["source-id"],"verdict":"supported",
 "statement":"Adjudicated requirement including exact values and exceptions",
 "rationale":"Evidence, strength, scope, and reason for judgment"}],
 "relations":[{"kind":"exception","finding_ids":["source-id","other-source-id"],
 "rationale":"Why these claims interact","resolution":"Result or unresolved dispute"}],
 "gaps":["Unresolved issue to escalate"]}
Allowed verdicts: supported, qualified, contradicted, unresolved.
Allowed relation kinds: support, contradiction, qualification, exception.

